#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/agricolainsert.py
msgid "AgricolaInsert"
msgstr "Inserto para Agricola"

#. description of AgricolaInsert
#: boxes/generators/agricolainsert.py
msgid ""
"\n"
"Agricola Revised Edition game box insert, including some expansions.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Inserto para la caja del juego Agricola Revised Edition, incluidas algunas expansiones.\n"

#. long description of AgricolaInsert in markdown
#: boxes/generators/agricolainsert.py
msgid ""
"\n"
"This insert was designed with 3 mm plywood in mind, and should work fine "
"with\n"
"materials around this thickness.\n"
"\n"
"This is an insert for the [Agricola Revised Edition](https://"
"boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/200680/agricola-revised-edition)\n"
"board game. It is specifically designed around the [Farmers Of The Moor "
"expansion](https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgameexpansion/257344/agricola-"
"farmers-moor),\n"
"and should also store the [5-6 players expansion](https://boardgamegeek.com/"
"boardgameexpansion/210625/agricola-expansion-5-and-6-players)\n"
"(not tested, but I tried to take everything into account for it, please "
"inform\n"
"us if you tested it).\n"
"\n"
"It can be stored inside the original game box, including the 2 expansions,\n"
"with the lid slightly raised.\n"
"\n"
"The parts of a given element are mostly generated next to each other "
"vertically.\n"
"It should be straightforward to match them.\n"
"\n"
"Here are the different elements, from left to right in the generated file.\n"
"\n"
"#### Card tray\n"
"\n"
"The cards are all kept in a tray, with paper dividers to sort them easily. "
"When\n"
"the tray is not full of cards, wood dividers slides in slots in order to "
"keep\n"
"the cards from falling into the empty space.\n"
"\n"
"There should be enough space for the main game, Farmers Of The Moor, and the "
"5-6\n"
"player expansion, but not much more than that.\n"
"\n"
"To keep a lower profile, the cards are at a slight angle, and the paper "
"dividers\n"
"tabs are horizontal instead of vertical.\n"
"A small wall keeps the card against one side while the tabs protrude on the\n"
"other side, above the small wall.\n"
"\n"
"The wall with the big hole is the sloped one. It goes between the two\n"
"\"comb-like\" walls first, with its two small holes at the bottom. Then "
"there is a\n"
"low-height long wall with a sloped edge which should go from the sloped wall "
"to\n"
"the other side. You can finish the tray with the last wall at the end.\n"
"\n"
"#### Upper level trays\n"
"\n"
"4 trays with movable walls are used to store resources. They were designed "
"to\n"
"store them in this order:\n"
"\n"
"* Stone / Vegetable / Pig / Cow\n"
"* Reed / Grain / Sheep\n"
"* Wood / Clay\n"
"* Food / Fire\n"
"\n"
"The wall would probably be better if fixed instead of movable, but I would "
"like\n"
"to test with the 5-6 player expansion to be sure their positions are "
"correct\n"
"with it too.\n"
"\n"
"The little feet of the movable wall should be glued. The triangles are put\n"
"horizontally, with their bases towards the sides.\n"
"\n"
"#### Lower level tray\n"
"\n"
"The lower level tray is used to store the horses.\n"
"\n"
"#### Room/Field tiles\n"
"\n"
"Two boxes are generated to store the room/field tiles. One for the wood/"
"field,\n"
"the other for the clay/stone. They are stored with the main opening upside, "
"but\n"
"I prefer to use them during play with this face on the side.\n"
"\n"
"#### Moor/Forest and miscellaneous tiles\n"
"\n"
"A box is generated to store the Moor/Forest tiles, and some other tiles such "
"as\n"
"the \"multiple resources\" cardboard tokens.\n"
"\n"
"The Moor/Forest tiles are at the same height as the Room/Field, and the "
"upper\n"
"level trays are directly on them. The horse box and player box are slightly\n"
"lower. This Moor/Forest box have a lowered corner (the one for the "
"miscellaneous\n"
"tiles). Two cardboard pieces can be stored between the smaller boxes and "
"the\n"
"upper level trays (as seen on the picture).\n"
"\n"
"Be sure to match the pieces so that the walls with smaller heights are next "
"to\n"
"each other.\n"
"\n"
"#### Players bit boxes\n"
"\n"
"Each player has its own box where the bits of his color are stored.\n"
"The cardboard bed from Farmers Of The Moor is central to this box.\n"
"\n"
"* The fences are stored inside the bed\n"
"* The bed is placed in the box, with holes to keep it there (and to take "
"less\n"
"  height)\n"
"* The stables are stored in the two corners\n"
"* The five farmers are stored between the bed and the three walls, "
"alternatively\n"
"  head up and head down.\n"
"\n"
"During assembly, the small bars are put in the middle holes. The two bigger\n"
"holes at the ends are used for the bed feet. The bar keeps the bed from\n"
"protruding underneath.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Este inserto se diseñó pensando en contrachapado de 3 mm y debería funcionar bien con\n"
"materiales de un grosor parecido.\n"
"\n"
"Es un inserto para el juego de mesa [Agricola Revised Edition](https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/200680/agricola-revised-edition).\n"
"Está diseñado específicamente en torno a la [expansión Farmers Of The Moor](https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgameexpansion/257344/agricola-farmers-moor)\n"
"y también debería dar cabida a la [expansión para 5-6 jugadores](https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgameexpansion/210625/agricola-expansion-5-and-6-players)\n"
"(sin probar, pero he intentado tenerlo todo en cuenta; avísanos si lo pruebas).\n"
"\n"
"Cabe dentro de la caja original del juego, con las 2 expansiones incluidas,\n"
"dejando la tapa ligeramente levantada.\n"
"\n"
"Las piezas de cada elemento se generan en su mayoría una junto a otra en vertical,\n"
"así que debería ser sencillo emparejarlas.\n"
"\n"
"Estos son los distintos elementos, de izquierda a derecha en el archivo generado.\n"
"\n"
"#### Bandeja de cartas\n"
"\n"
"Todas las cartas se guardan en una bandeja, con separadores de papel para ordenarlas\n"
"fácilmente. Cuando la bandeja no está llena de cartas, unos separadores de madera se\n"
"deslizan por unas ranuras para evitar que las cartas se caigan al hueco vacío.\n"
"\n"
"Debería haber sitio suficiente para el juego base, Farmers Of The Moor y la expansión\n"
"para 5-6 jugadores, pero no mucho más.\n"
"\n"
"Para reducir la altura, las cartas van ligeramente inclinadas y las pestañas de los\n"
"separadores de papel son horizontales en lugar de verticales.\n"
"Una pared pequeña mantiene las cartas contra un lado, mientras que las pestañas\n"
"sobresalen por el otro, por encima de esa pared.\n"
"\n"
"La pared con el agujero grande es la inclinada. Va entre las dos paredes «en forma de\n"
"peine», con sus dos agujeros pequeños abajo. Después hay una pared larga y baja con un\n"
"canto inclinado que debe ir desde la pared inclinada hasta el otro lado. Puedes rematar\n"
"la bandeja con la última pared al final.\n"
"\n"
"#### Bandejas del nivel superior\n"
"\n"
"Se usan 4 bandejas con paredes móviles para guardar los recursos. Están diseñadas para\n"
"guardarlos en este orden:\n"
"\n"
"* Piedra / Verdura / Cerdo / Vaca\n"
"* Junco / Grano / Oveja\n"
"* Madera / Arcilla\n"
"* Comida / Fuego\n"
"\n"
"Probablemente la pared quedaría mejor fija en lugar de móvil, pero me gustaría probarlo\n"
"con la expansión para 5-6 jugadores para asegurarme de que las posiciones también son\n"
"correctas con ella.\n"
"\n"
"Los piececitos de la pared móvil hay que encolarlos. Los triángulos se colocan en\n"
"horizontal, con la base hacia los lados.\n"
"\n"
"#### Bandeja del nivel inferior\n"
"\n"
"La bandeja del nivel inferior se usa para guardar los caballos.\n"
"\n"
"#### Losetas de habitación y campo\n"
"\n"
"Se generan dos cajas para guardar las losetas de habitación y campo: una para las de\n"
"madera y campo y otra para las de arcilla y piedra. Se guardan con la abertura principal\n"
"hacia arriba, aunque yo prefiero usarlas durante la partida con esa cara hacia un lado.\n"
"\n"
"#### Losetas de páramo, bosque y varios\n"
"\n"
"Se genera una caja para guardar las losetas de páramo y bosque, junto con otras fichas,\n"
"como los marcadores de cartón de «recursos múltiples».\n"
"\n"
"Las losetas de páramo y bosque quedan a la misma altura que las de habitación y campo, y\n"
"las bandejas del nivel superior van directamente encima de ellas. La caja de los caballos\n"
"y la de los jugadores quedan algo más bajas. Esta caja de páramo y bosque tiene una\n"
"esquina rebajada (la de las losetas variadas). Entre las cajas pequeñas y las bandejas\n"
"del nivel superior se pueden guardar dos piezas de cartón (como se ve en la foto).\n"
"\n"
"Asegúrate de emparejar las piezas de forma que las paredes de menor altura queden juntas.\n"
"\n"
"#### Cajas de piezas de los jugadores\n"
"\n"
"Cada jugador tiene su propia caja para guardar las piezas de su color.\n"
"La cama de cartón de Farmers Of The Moor es el elemento central de esta caja.\n"
"\n"
"* Las vallas se guardan dentro de la cama\n"
"* La cama se coloca en la caja, con agujeros que la mantienen en su sitio (y que hacen\n"
"  que ocupe menos altura)\n"
"* Los establos se guardan en las dos esquinas\n"
"* Los cinco granjeros se guardan entre la cama y las tres paredes, alternando cabeza\n"
"  arriba y cabeza abajo.\n"
"\n"
"Durante el montaje, las barritas se colocan en los agujeros centrales. Los dos agujeros\n"
"mayores de los extremos son para las patas de la cama. La barra evita que la cama\n"
"sobresalga por debajo.\n"
"\n"

