#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/frontpanel.py
msgid "FrontPanel"
msgstr "Panel frontal"

#. description of FrontPanel
#: boxes/generators/frontpanel.py
msgid "Mounting Holes and cutouts for all your holy needs."
msgstr "Agujeros de montaje y recortes para todas tus necesidades perforadoras."

#. long description of FrontPanel in markdown
#: boxes/generators/frontpanel.py
msgid ""
"\n"
"<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://md-block.verou.me/md-block.js\"></"
"script>\n"
"<md-block>\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This will help you create font (and side and top) panels for your\n"
"boxes that are pre-configured for all the bits and bobs you'd like to\n"
"install\n"
"\n"
"    The layout can create several types of holes including rectangles,\n"
"    circles and mounting holes.  The default shows an example layout with "
"all\n"
"    currently supported objects.\n"
"\n"
"####\n"
"`rect x y w h [cr=0] [cx=True] [cy=True]`\n"
"\n"
"     x: x position\n"
"     y: y position\n"
"     w: width\n"
"     h: height\n"
"    cr: optional, Corner radius, default=0\n"
"    cx: optional, Center x.  the x position denotes the center of the "
"rectangle.\n"
"        accepts t, T, 1, or other true-like values.\n"
"    cy: optional, Center y.  the y position denotes the center of the "
"rectangle.\n"
"\n"
"#### outline\n"
"`rect w h`\n"
"\n"
"    w: width\n"
"    h: height\n"
"\n"
"`outline` has a special meaning: You can create multiple panel outlines with "
"one command.\n"
"This has the effect of making it easy to manage all the holes on all the "
"sides of\n"
"your boxes.\n"
"\n"
"#### circle\n"
"`circle x y r`\n"
"\n"
"    x: x position\n"
"    y: y position\n"
"    r: radius\n"
"\n"
"#### mountinghole\n"
"mountinghole x y d_shaft [d_head=0] [angle=0]\n"
"\n"
"          x: x position\n"
"          y: y position\n"
"    d_shaft: diameter of the shaft part of the mounting hole\n"
"     d_head: optional. diameter of the head\n"
"      angle: optional. angle of the mounting hole\n"
"\n"
"#### text\n"
"`text x y size \"some text\" [angle=0] [align=bottom|left]`\n"
"\n"
"        x: x position\n"
"        y: y position\n"
"     size: size, in mm\n"
"     text: text to render.  This *must* be in quotation marks\n"
"    angle: angle (in degrees)\n"
"    align: string with combinations of (top|middle|bottom) and (left|center|"
"right),\n"
"           separated by '|'.  Default is 'bottom|left'\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#### nema\n"
"`nema x y size [screwhole_size=0]`\n"
"\n"
"        x: x position (center of shaft)\n"
"        y: y position (center of shaft)\n"
"     size: nema size.  One of [8, 11, 14, 16, 17, 23, 24, 34, 42]\n"
"    screw: screw size, in mm.  Optional.  Default=0, which means the default "
"size\n"
"</md-block>\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://md-block.verou.me/md-block.js\"></script>\n"
"<md-block>\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Esto te ayuda a crear paneles frontales (y laterales y superiores) para tus\n"
"cajas, ya preparados para todos los cacharros que quieras\n"
"instalar\n"
"\n"
"    La distribución puede crear varios tipos de agujeros: rectángulos,\n"
"    círculos y agujeros de montaje. El valor predeterminado muestra un ejemplo\n"
"    con todos los objetos admitidos actualmente.\n"
"\n"
"####\n"
"`rect x y w h [cr=0] [cx=True] [cy=True]`\n"
"\n"
"     x: posición X\n"
"     y: posición Y\n"
"     w: anchura\n"
"     h: altura\n"
"    cr: opcional, radio de esquina, predeterminado=0\n"
"    cx: opcional, centrar en X. La posición X indica el centro del rectángulo.\n"
"        acepta t, T, 1 u otros valores equivalentes a «verdadero».\n"
"    cy: opcional, centrar en Y. La posición Y indica el centro del rectángulo.\n"
"\n"
"#### outline\n"
"`rect w h`\n"
"\n"
"    w: anchura\n"
"    h: altura\n"
"\n"
"`outline` tiene un significado especial: permite crear varios contornos de panel con una sola orden.\n"
"Así resulta fácil gestionar todos los agujeros de todos los lados de\n"
"tus cajas.\n"
"\n"
"#### circle\n"
"`circle x y r`\n"
"\n"
"    x: posición X\n"
"    y: posición Y\n"
"    r: radio\n"
"\n"
"#### mountinghole\n"
"mountinghole x y d_shaft [d_head=0] [angle=0]\n"
"\n"
"          x: posición X\n"
"          y: posición Y\n"
"    d_shaft: diámetro del vástago del agujero de montaje\n"
"     d_head: opcional. Diámetro de la cabeza\n"
"      angle: opcional. Ángulo del agujero de montaje\n"
"\n"
"#### text\n"
"`text x y size \"some text\" [angle=0] [align=bottom|left]`\n"
"\n"
"        x: posición X\n"
"        y: posición Y\n"
"     size: tamaño, en mm\n"
"     text: texto que se dibujará. *Tiene* que ir entre comillas\n"
"    angle: ángulo (en grados)\n"
"    align: cadena con combinaciones de (top|middle|bottom) y (left|center|right),\n"
"           separadas por «|». El valor predeterminado es 'bottom|left'\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"#### nema\n"
"`nema x y size [screwhole_size=0]`\n"
"\n"
"        x: posición X (centro del eje)\n"
"        y: posición Y (centro del eje)\n"
"     size: tamaño Nema. Uno de [8, 11, 14, 16, 17, 23, 24, 34, 42]\n"
"    screw: tamaño del tornillo, en mm. Opcional. Predeterminado=0, que significa el tamaño por omisión\n"
"</md-block>\n"
"    "

msgid "FrontPanel Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes del panel frontal"

