msgid "RoyalGame"
msgstr "Juego real de Ur"

#. description of RoyalGame
#: boxes/generators/royalgame.py
msgid "The Royal Game of Ur"
msgstr "El Juego Real de Ur"

#. long description of RoyalGame in markdown
#: boxes/generators/royalgame.py
msgid ""
"Most of the blue lines need to be engraved by cutting with high speed and "
"low power. But there are three blue holes that actually need to be cut: The "
"grip hole in the lid and two tiny rectangles on the top and bottom for the "
"lid to grip into.\n"
"\n"
"![Lid Details](static/samples/RoyalGame-2.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"![All pieces](static/samples/RoyalGame-3.jpg)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"La mayoría de las líneas azules hay que grabarlas cortando a alta velocidad y baja potencia. Pero hay tres huecos azules que sí hay que cortar de verdad: el agujero de agarre de la tapa y dos rectángulos diminutos arriba y abajo donde encaja la tapa.\n"
"\n"
"![Detalles de la tapa](static/samples/RoyalGame-2.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"![Todas las piezas](static/samples/RoyalGame-3.jpg)\n"
"\n"

msgid "RoyalGame Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes del Juego Real de Ur"

#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid "SevenSegmentPattern"
msgstr "Patrón de siete segmentos"

#. description of SevenSegmentPattern
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid "Holepatterns and walls for a seven segment digit"
msgstr "Patrones de agujeros y paredes para un dígito de siete segmentos"

#. long description of SevenSegmentPattern in markdown
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid ""
"This pattern is indented to be used with a LED stripe that is wound through "
"all segments in an S pattern while the stripe being upright on its side. It "
"can also be used with small pieces of LED stripes connected with short wires "
"for large enough sizes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este patrón está pensado para usarse con una tira de LED que recorre todos los segmentos en zigzag, colocada de canto. Para tamaños suficientemente grandes también se puede usar con trozos pequeños de tira de LED unidos con cables cortos.\n"

msgid "SevenSegmentPattern Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes del patrón de siete segmentos"

#. parameter name
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid "digit"
msgstr "dígito"

#. help for parameter digit
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid "height of the digit (without walls) in mm"
msgstr "altura del dígito (sin las paredes) en mm"

#. help for parameter h
#: boxes/generators/sevensegment.py
msgid "height separation walls in mm"
msgstr "altura de las paredes de separación en mm"

#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/sevensegmentclock.py
msgid "SevenSegmentClock"
msgstr "Reloj de siete segmentos"

#. description of SevenSegmentClock
#: boxes/generators/sevensegmentclock.py
msgid "Seven segment clock build with LED stripe"
msgstr "Reloj de siete segmentos construido con tira de LED"

#. long description of SevenSegmentClock in markdown
#: boxes/generators/sevensegmentclock.py
msgid ""
"You need a LED stripe that is wound through all segments in an S pattern and "
"then continuing to the next digit while the stripe being upright on its "
"side. Selecting *debug* gives a better idea how things fit together.\n"
"\n"
"Adding a diffuser on top or at the bottom of the segment holes will probably "
"enhance the visuals. Just using paper may be enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"Necesitas una tira de LED que recorra en zigzag todos los segmentos y siga hasta el dígito siguiente, colocada de canto. Activar *debug* ayuda a entender mejor cómo encaja todo.\n"
"\n"
"Poner un difusor encima o debajo de los agujeros de los segmentos seguramente mejore el resultado visual. Con papel puede bastar.\n"

msgid "SevenSegmentClock Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes del reloj de siete segmentos"

#. help for parameter height
#: boxes/generators/sevensegmentclock.py
msgid "height of the front panel (with walls if outside is selected) in mm"
msgstr "altura del panel frontal (con las paredes si se marca «exterior») en mm"

#. help for parameter h
#: boxes/generators/sevensegmentclock.py
msgid "depth (with walls if outside is selected) in mm"
msgstr "profundidad (con las paredes si se marca «exterior») en mm"

