#. name of box generator
#: boxes/generators/trayinsert.py
msgid "TrayInsert"
msgstr "Inserto para bandeja"

#. description of TrayInsert
#: boxes/generators/trayinsert.py
msgid ""
"Tray insert without floor and outer walls - allows only continuous walls"
msgstr "Inserto para bandeja sin fondo ni paredes exteriores: solo admite paredes continuas"

#. long description of TrayInsert in markdown
#: boxes/generators/trayinsert.py
msgid ""
"## Tray/Box insert dividers.\n"
"Tray insert with extra margin for that perfect fit.\n"
"\n"
"You can specify the grid sizes with the standard `(sx, sy)` format, which "
"allows nice\n"
"variable rows and columns.  If you  check the `outside` box, the full "
"outside of the\n"
"tray insert ends up being the sum of all the sx/sy values.  However, if you "
"want a\n"
"consistent cell size, and uncheck outside, then the overall dimensions end "
"up\n"
"larger by `(n-1)*thickness`, to make space for your walls.\n"
"\n"
"You can specify the `x` and `y` parameters if you like, just make them "
"larger than\n"
"what the sum of `(sx, sy)` would end up with, and the walls be automatically "
"extended to\n"
"to exactly fill the inside of your tray or box.\n"
"\n"
"So, for example, if you're fitting `30mm x 40mm` items and want them to\n"
"fit inside a `250mm x 300mm` box, you can specify\n"
"\n"
"    sx = 30*8\n"
"    sy = 40*7\n"
"    uncheck outside\n"
"    x=250\n"
"    y=300\n"
"\n"
"This frees your mind into separately thinking about the cell size vs the "
"overall box size.\n"
"\n"
"![Tray Extra](static/samples/TrayInsert-3.jpg)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"## Separadores para insertar en una bandeja o caja.\n"
"Inserto para bandeja con margen adicional para que encaje a la perfección.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes indicar los tamaños de la retícula con el formato estándar `(sx, sy)`, que permite\n"
"filas y columnas de distinto tamaño. Si marcas la casilla `outside`, el exterior completo\n"
"del inserto acaba siendo la suma de todos los valores de sx/sy. En cambio, si quieres un\n"
"tamaño de celda constante y desmarcas `outside`, las dimensiones totales aumentan en\n"
"`(n-1)*thickness` para dejar sitio a las paredes.\n"
"\n"
"Si quieres, puedes indicar los parámetros `x` e `y`: basta con que sean mayores que la suma\n"
"de `(sx, sy)`, y las paredes se prolongarán automáticamente para llenar exactamente el\n"
"interior de tu bandeja o caja.\n"
"\n"
"Por ejemplo, si vas a colocar objetos de `30mm x 40mm` y quieres que quepan\n"
"dentro de una caja de `250mm x 300mm`, puedes indicar\n"
"\n"
"    sx = 30*8\n"
"    sy = 40*7\n"
"    desmarcar outside\n"
"    x=250\n"
"    y=300\n"
"\n"
"Así puedes pensar por separado en el tamaño de la celda y en el tamaño total de la caja.\n"
"\n"
"![Inserto para bandeja](static/samples/TrayInsert-3.jpg)\n"
"    "

msgid "TrayInsert Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes del inserto para bandeja"

